WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.141 --> 00:00:03.529
- [Voiceover] It's 5:35 in the morning.

00:00:03.529 --> 00:00:05.508
- You should never wake up in darkness

00:00:05.508 --> 00:00:07.180
if the sun isn't out, that's a sign

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:09.409
that whatever you're
doing, it's not worth it.

00:00:09.409 --> 00:00:11.429
- I just got in my car, I'm pretty tired.

00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:14.865
- And I am on my way to a dance party.

00:00:14.865 --> 00:00:16.986
- Why?

00:00:18.603 --> 00:00:23.311
(techno music)

00:00:23.944 --> 00:00:25.314
- I've been to a couple of these before

00:00:25.314 --> 00:00:26.800
and I thought they were really fun

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.002
so I told Jen and Maycie
and Ryan from the Testies,

00:00:31.002 --> 00:00:32.953
or the Test Friends, but
I call 'em the Testies

00:00:32.953 --> 00:00:34.880
'cause it's a great name,

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.248
and Zach from the Try Guys.

00:00:37.248 --> 00:00:39.616
I invited them to come to this party

00:00:39.616 --> 00:00:41.033
to see what they think of it.

00:00:41.033 --> 00:00:42.333
- I think I can do this.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:44.260
Gonna go, we're gonna try and dance.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:46.187
- It's actually crazy,
there are so many cars

00:00:46.187 --> 00:00:48.765
and so many people, and
I don't understand why.

00:00:48.765 --> 00:00:52.864
- It is 6:35 in the
morning, we're gonna dance

00:00:52.864 --> 00:00:54.152
and then we're gonna go to work,

00:00:54.152 --> 00:00:55.390
and it's gonna be fucking awesome.

00:00:59.336 --> 00:01:00.219
- Tired.

00:01:00.219 --> 00:01:02.611
- I feel okay, I don't really
like dance parties at night.

00:01:02.611 --> 00:01:03.323
- No, yeah.

00:01:05.248 --> 00:01:05.988
- Well

00:01:05.988 --> 00:01:07.278
- Yeah, ehh

00:01:07.278 --> 00:01:09.089
- I don't know, it just feels weird,

00:01:09.089 --> 00:01:11.450
like why do people do this?

00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:13.284
- I feel like the only
people who wake up early

00:01:13.284 --> 00:01:16.078
to go dancing are like
beautiful, fit people.

00:01:17.819 --> 00:01:18.648
And Henry.

00:01:18.648 --> 00:01:21.534
- This is probably the
weirdest / silliest thing

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:24.924
I've ever done on a work
day, it's a Tuesday.

00:01:24.963 --> 00:01:29.266
(techno music)

00:01:29.945 --> 00:01:32.974
- Daybreaker started about a
year and a half ago in New York

00:01:32.974 --> 00:01:36.143
and then it's almost our
one year anniversary in LA.

00:01:36.143 --> 00:01:39.800
It's a way to get people
out of their normal routine

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.518
to have fun in the morning,
and then go to work

00:01:41.518 --> 00:01:43.329
and change the world.

00:01:43.329 --> 00:01:44.932
- This gathering is just about,

00:01:44.932 --> 00:01:46.580
the energy that we create together

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:49.181
to supercharge our day, our week, our life

00:01:49.181 --> 00:01:51.851
it's not serious, it's
just fun for everyone.

00:01:51.851 --> 00:01:53.205
(techno music)

00:01:59.805 --> 00:02:02.195
(techno music)

00:02:04.345 --> 00:02:04.885
(Maycie laughs)

00:02:04.885 --> 00:02:05.771
- It's incredible

00:02:05.771 --> 00:02:06.612
- It's pretty amazing

00:02:06.612 --> 00:02:08.702
- Oh yeah, facepaint and bodypaint on us,

00:02:08.702 --> 00:02:09.631
which is pretty rad.

00:02:09.631 --> 00:02:11.790
- I feel like it looks
kinda cool, so I'm into it.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.833
- I haven't had coffee
today, but I feel great

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.110
- [Voicover] You know
there's coffee in there

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:15.668
- I don't care

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.106
- Yeah, we had weird watermelon
rind drink, pretty good

00:02:18.106 --> 00:02:19.360
- Yeah, I had watermelon
juice instead of coffee

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.356
because I wanted to challenge
myself, like do I need coffee?

00:02:21.356 --> 00:02:23.910
No, I wanna be energized
by dance, and guess what?

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.793
I am.

00:02:24.793 --> 00:02:26.023
- I just want to say that right now

00:02:26.023 --> 00:02:28.183
I'd normally be just getting
up and feeling super groggy,

00:02:28.183 --> 00:02:30.574
and I feel incredible right now instead.

00:02:31.244 --> 00:02:34.359
- Yeah, I wouldn't even be
getting up for 20 more minutes.

00:02:34.359 --> 00:02:37.501
- You would think, it's light
out so people are judging,

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:39.490
but because it's light
out I think it's just

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.348
come as you are, who
cares, have a good time.

00:02:41.348 --> 00:02:42.648
People are really accepting in there!

00:02:42.648 --> 00:02:45.202
We joined a dance line, and
there were these awesome dancers

00:02:45.202 --> 00:02:47.855
teaching us dance moves, I
learned this thing, pretty cool

00:02:47.855 --> 00:02:49.033
- Yeah I didn't really keep up with it.

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.629
- Nah I got it, I got this, I'm good.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.157
- I definitely wouldn't
describe this as a rave

00:02:54.157 --> 00:02:55.883
it's almost like a work
out class in the morning

00:02:55.883 --> 00:02:57.044
but with dancing.

00:02:57.044 --> 00:02:59.993
- It seems to be a more
genuine, positive time

00:02:59.993 --> 00:03:03.197
I did not see a single
person grind up on a girl

00:03:03.197 --> 00:03:04.985
and like try and do that,
except for right now

00:03:04.985 --> 00:03:05.962
now it's happening.

00:03:05.962 --> 00:03:06.889
- Not for lack of trying.

00:03:06.889 --> 00:03:09.211
We tried to make it happen
earlier, it didn't work.

00:03:09.211 --> 00:03:10.697
- Blanketly describing it,
'cause I'm gonna be like

00:03:10.697 --> 00:03:14.389
there's this really crazy,
sober, 6 am dance party

00:03:14.909 --> 00:03:16.943
it sounds really weird,
it is really weird,

00:03:16.943 --> 00:03:19.427
but you should try it,
'cause it's also really fun.

00:03:19.427 --> 00:03:21.935
- I feel great, I feel like I
enjoyed it more than you did.

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:23.398
- You know what, I think what it is

00:03:23.398 --> 00:03:25.023
is for me, you have to be able to dance,

00:03:25.023 --> 00:03:27.484
you have to like, be not
self conscious at all,

00:03:27.484 --> 00:03:30.251
and I'm not sure I'm there
necessarily when I'm sober.

00:03:31.552 --> 00:03:33.183
- I saw a new side of Henry Goldman today

00:03:33.183 --> 00:03:34.738
I did not know he had those moves,

00:03:34.738 --> 00:03:36.503
he busted 'em out, it was pretty rad.

00:03:36.503 --> 00:03:38.012
- It takes a special kind of person

00:03:38.012 --> 00:03:39.754
to be able to get up very early,

00:03:39.754 --> 00:03:41.379
come to a dance party and just let loose.

00:03:41.379 --> 00:03:42.122
- Yeah, us.

00:03:42.122 --> 00:03:44.090
- Yeah, this type of person!

00:03:44.276 --> 00:03:48.084
(people cheering)

00:03:49.041 --> 00:03:52.472
- I'm dancing sober as fuck
at 6:30 in the morning.

